<title>SWITZERLAND: ABB AG Q1 EPS up to 19.25 Sfr.</title>
<headline>ABB AG Q1 EPS up to 19.25 Sfr.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electrical engineering group ABB Asea Brown Boveri AG said first quarter net income per bearer share of ABB AG, the Swiss holding company that owns half of the ABB Group, rose to 19.25 Swiss francs from 14.80 francs.</p>
<p>ABB said in a statement that ABB AG's share of ABB Group earnings before taxes for the first quarter amounted to $194 million, an increase of six percent.</p>
<p>After translation into Swiss francs, ABB AG's share of earnings before taxes amounted to 276 million francs, up from 218 million.</p>
<p>Net income for ABB AG rose 32 percent to 178 million from 135 million.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
